---
/**
 * The member's theme before first paint, on every layout: `lib/theme.ts`
 * remembers a forced light or dark choice in `kinship.theme`, and this script
 * applies it before the stylesheet's tokens resolve. Without a saved choice
 * the tokens follow the OS. Public and sign-in pages read the same key, so the
 * choice a member made inside the app survives signing out.
 *
 * The body's whitespace is part of the gateway CSP's `sha256-` hash
 * (`gateway/security_headers.conf`); keep it byte for byte.
 */
---

<script is:inline>
      try {
        const theme = localStorage.getItem("kinship.theme");
        if (theme === "light" || theme === "dark") {
          document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
        }
      } catch {}
    </script>
